  "notes": "Create binds the native trigger compiler with its review (SQL mode identity and MySQL Shell 9.7 grammar). MySQL has no ALTER TRIGGER and the editor does not recreate one (Decision 9 default; replacement stays an explicit DROP/CREATE or DDN workflow), so a reopened trigger shows its stored properties locked: name, database, table, timing, event, body and definer pre-fill from the inspected record. IF NOT EXISTS and FOLLOWS/PRECEDES are creation options (the catalog keeps only ACTION_ORDER). Round-tripped 2026-11-05 on the MySQL 9.7.0 demo (tools/tests/test_ui_descriptor_roundtrip_mysql.py): every field set, order and definer read back, and reopened values pre-filled."
